<title>SINGAPORE: Presscrete full year profit up 32.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Presscrete full year profit up 32.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Nov 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				1.61 vs 1.36</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			 4.0 vs nil</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     3.32 vs 2.94</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)     NA vs NA</p>
<p>    Turnover				 19.61 vs 11.83</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.18 vs 0.17</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.12 vs 0.04</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		0.94 vs 0.53</p>
<p>    Profits from associates		nil vs nil</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  2.43 vs 1.83</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.75 vs 0.50</p>
<p>    Minorities		     (loss) 0.07 vs 0.03 (gain)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			  nil vs nil</p>
<p>Note - Presscrete Holdings said pre-tax profit rose 32.3 percent in 1996 on 1995, about five to nine percent above forecasts given in the prospectus for the company's initial public offering in September 1996. It said the date for dividend payments would be set later.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
